  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Branch (constraint 1); declare STANDARD rigor plus code-review and adr-check (TEST-MODIFYING).</step>
    <step order="1">A1 `RouteCreate_AnEventUnderATeamOwnedEventOfASecureMatter_IsOwnedByTheEventsOrdinaryTeam_DI009Window`: world `.WithSecureRoot("sprk_matter", SecureMatter)`; the parent Event team-owned by ChildTeam in ChildBu and filed under SecureMatter; the stamp world derives sprk_regardingmatter = SecureMatter. Comment names #2483 and says 042b inverts the test.</step>
    <step order="2">A2 (same file): build the written row from A1's create body and ask the same resolver ForExistingRowAsync → ResolveOwnerAsync.</step>
    <step order="3">A3 (seam file): the same world as the system principal.</step>
    <step order="4">AC3's scratch check, never committed. Run the filtered suites; update TASK-INDEX to `✅ [done]`; record in notes/task-042a-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If A1 does NOT reproduce the window on the current src (the create is already owned by SecureNamedTeam), STOP and escalate: the defect premise of §15.1 is false and 042b must be re-scoped.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a test can only pass by changing a file under src/, STOP and escalate rather than changing it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/data-mutation/RecordOwnership/RouteCreatePreCreateStampTests.cs</output>
