  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">AC1: A1, A2 and A3 are added and pass on the current src/; `git diff --stat` against the branch base lists no path under src/.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC2: A1 asserts all four facts: 201; `ownerid@odata.bind` = `/teams(ChildTeam)`; `sprk_RegardingMatter@odata.bind` = `/sprk_matters(SecureMatter)` in the create body; no sharee-mirror row for the new event.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC3: A2 asserts that the reconciler's question over A1's written row resolves to SecureNamedTeam (the window's disagreement in one assertion).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC4: A3, as the system principal, asserts an ordinary owner, no stamp in the create body, and the stamp bound by the post-create re-derivation (as the existing test at ~:44-62 asserts it).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC5 (negative): A1 fails when ResolveOwnerOverAsync is given the derived stamp. Verified once by a local scratch edit to src that is never committed; the edit, the failing assertion and the revert are recorded in the notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC6 (negative): ChatCreatedChildStampTests.cs ~:106 (the ordinary control) is unchanged and green; no existing test in the two modified files changes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC7: the filtered suites SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests*, RecordCreationServicePipelineSeamTests* and ChatCreatedChildStampTests pass; code-review and adr-check results are in the notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: exactly the three characterizations above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

